.TH UNIWIFI.TOML 5 "October 2026" "uniwifi 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
uniwifi.toml \- configuration file for the UniWiFi AutoLogin daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fI~/.config/uniwifi/config.toml\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBuniwifi.toml\fR file defines daemon polling parameters, Wi-Fi SSID allowlists,
captive portal endpoint targets, and security policies for \fBuniwifi\fR(1).
.PP
The configuration file is formatted in TOML syntax. Permissions on this file must be strictly
set to \fB0600\fR (\fIrw-------\fR); world-readable or group-readable permissions will be flagged
by \fBuniwifi config audit\fR.

.SH SECTIONS
.SS [general]
The general section controls network polling, SSID allowlisting, and retry behavior.
.TP
.B ssids
Array of strings representing the wireless network SSIDs for which auto-login should be attempted.
Example: \fBssids = ["Campus-WiFi", "eduroam-guest"]\fR
.TP
.B check_url
The plain HTTP probe URL used to detect captive portal interception.
Default: \fB"http://fedoraproject.org/static/hotspot.txt"\fR
.TP
.B check_expect
Expected body content from \fBcheck_url\fR indicating genuine internet connectivity.
Default: \fB"OK"\fR
.TP
.B probe_timeout
Network probe HTTP request timeout in seconds.
Default: \fB6.0\fR
.TP
.B max_attempts
Maximum login retry attempts before backing off.
Default: \fB4\fR
.TP
.B base_delay
Initial exponential backoff delay in seconds.
Default: \fB5.0\fR
.TP
.B max_delay
Maximum exponential backoff delay in seconds.
Default: \fB60.0\fR
.TP
.B notify
Boolean indicating whether to dispatch desktop notifications on successful login.
Default: \fBtrue\fR
.TP
.B notify_on_failure
Boolean indicating whether to dispatch desktop notifications on authentication failure.
Default: \fBtrue\fR

.SS [portal]
The portal section defines authentication modes and security constraints.
.TP
.B mode
Authentication engine mode: \fB"form"\fR (HTML autodetection), \fB"custom"\fR (manual field mapping),
or \fB"browser"\fR (headless Playwright browser).
Default: \fB"form"\fR
.TP
.B allowed_hosts
Array of trusted domain hostnames permitted for form action submission. Mitigates rogue access point
phishing attacks.
Example: \fBallowed_hosts = ["portal.campus.edu", "auth.university.edu"]\fR
.TP
.B allow_insecure_http
Boolean indicating whether plain \fBhttp://\fR endpoints are permitted for credential submission.
Default: \fBfalse\fR (HTTPS is strictly enforced).
.TP
.B login_url
Explicit login action endpoint when \fBmode = "custom"\fR.
.TP
.B method
HTTP method for credential submission (\fB"POST"\fR or \fB"GET"\fR).
Default: \fB"POST"\fR
.TP
.B username_field
Form field name for the username in custom mode.
.TP
.B password_field
Form field name for the password in custom mode.

.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Passwords are never stored in \fBuniwifi.toml\fR. They must always be stored in the OS keyring
via \fBuniwifi setup\fR.

.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[general]
ssids = ["Campus-WiFi"]
check_url = "http://fedoraproject.org/static/hotspot.txt"
check_expect = "OK"
notify = true

[portal]
mode = "form"
allowed_hosts = ["portal.campus.edu"]
allow_insecure_http = false
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
